From be0e9488021a0d35a3c884b80bd4a6ac23f2dfea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yongqin Wang <yongqinwang@roblox.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 17:56:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] [Spec Decode] Support speculative decoding under pipeline
 parallelism

Speculative decoding and pipeline parallelism could not be combined. Two
things stood in the way. The drafter consumes auxiliary hidden states
tapped from layers that, under PP, live on stages other than the one that
runs the draft model. And ranks other than the last never see the draft
tokens, so they cannot embed the right ids on the following step.

Carry the aux taps on the pipeline handoff that already exists. Each stage
packs its own taps into the IntermediateTensors it is about to send, at
globally numbered slots derived from the layer split, and passes the
upstream taps along with them; the last rank then reads fixed slots. No
stage has to negotiate the layout, because every stage derives the same
numbering from the split. Packing is pure data movement with no collective
inside the forward, so the model stays capturable by full CUDA graphs.

Broadcast the draft proposals from the last rank so earlier stages can
embed real token ids, reusing the deferred sample slot so a single event
covers both the sampled tokens and the drafts.

Run the drafter on the last stage only rather than inheriting the target's
PP size, which previously required the draft architecture to implement
SupportsPP, and drop the config gate that refused EAGLE3 under PP.

Covers Eagle3 and DSpark drafting for Llama, Qwen2/Qwen3, DeepSeek-V4 and
Kimi-K3.

Signed-off-by: Yongqin Wang <yongqinwang@roblox.com>
